    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0890" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg848"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 396</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.10/4–2551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Spain
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d396-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-27T15:00:00-05:00">April 27, 1951—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>741. Urtel 958 Apr 25.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d396-f2"/> Carry-over to next fiscal
                    year of funds for loans to Spain suggested and approved by Pres. Ltr and doc re
                    this action has been air pouched to you. This info shld not be communicated in
                    any form to Spans. After admin steps have been taken to carry out action
                    approved by Pres, you will be instructed re informing Spans.</p>
                <p>Action re removing limitation being taken and it is therefore unnecessary you
                    communicate directly with Pres this subj.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d396-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d396-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Dunham and cleared with Sauer
                    of the Export-Import Bank, Corbett of the
                    Office of Financial and Development Policy, and Tannenwald of the Office of the
                    Special Assistant to the President, Averell
                        Harriman.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d396-f2" n="2" xml:id="d396-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Griffis had asked in this
                    telegram if the $25 million loan limitation with respect to Spain was still in
                    effect and added that it appeared that the Spanish Government knew nothing of
                    this limitation. (852.10/4–2551)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
